    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.jump\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.x\n\n### Description\n\nI'm not sure what's causing the issue, so here's a loose collection of facts:\n\n- I switch ; and : in my config\n- I previously had mini.jump installed standalone, but just now consolidated all my mini plugins into one mini.nvim installation (via lazy)\n- when standalone, mini.jump was calling setup with no additional config\n\nPreviously, everything worked great! Now, pressing `;` gives me `(mini.jump) Can not jump because there is no recent target.` I tried rebinding a la `mappings = { repeat_jump = ''` but no dice.\n\nNow I have no way to access command mode. I never thought the \"can't quit vim\" joke would happen to me...\n\n### Reproduction\n\ninit.lua:\n```\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\nlocal clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim', mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\nvim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\n\nvim.keymap.set('n', ';', ':', {noremap = true, silent = false})\nvim.keymap.set('n', ':', ';', {noremap = true, silent = true})\n\nrequire('mini.jump').setup { mappings = {repeat_jump = ''}}\n```",
